From 49abd74ae1bfeaa73313c300e33482464b6e1c79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Clarke <sanity@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Mar 2026 09:02:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 33/69] fix(ui): render message content in div instead of span
 for valid HTML
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The markdown-to-HTML conversion wraps messages in <p> tags (block
elements), but they were rendered inside a <span> (inline element).
This is invalid HTML — browsers close the span before the <p>,
breaking rendering of block content including line breaks (<br />).

Changing the container from span to div makes the nesting valid and
restores newline rendering in messages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ui/src/components/conversation.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ui/src/components/conversation.rs b/ui/src/components/conversation.rs
index 629b3687..57fc363d 100644
--- a/ui/src/components/conversation.rs
+++ b/ui/src/components/conversation.rs
@@ -1491,7 +1491,7 @@ fn MessageGroupComponent(
                                                             }
                                                         }
                                                     },
-                                                    span {
+                                                    div {
                                                         class: "prose prose-sm dark:prose-invert max-w-none",
                                                         dangerous_inner_html: "{msg.content_html}"
                                                     }
-- 
2.53.0

